    '**Between characters.** The rich man, Lazarus, the angels, Abraham and the five brethren are distinct. Lazarus is named; the rich man is not. Jesus identifies none of them.',
    '**Between speakers.** The rich man speaks at 16:24, 27–28 and 30. Abraham speaks at 16:25–26, 29 and 31. Their words are the words of persons in the account and are not Jesus’ statement of what the account means.',
    '**Between settings.** The account stands in Luke 16 after the steward and the Pharisees’ derision. The Rich Fool stands in Luke 12 and the Lost Son in Luke 15.',
    '**Between this account and its neighbors.** The gate, the sores, the gulf and Moses and the prophets belong to this account only. Mammon and the steward’s debtors belong to 16:1–13. The barns and God’s words in the night belong to the Rich Fool. The far country and the feast belong to the Lost Son.',
    '**What must not be assigned.** No identity for the rich man, Lazarus, Abraham, the angels, the five brethren, the gulf or the place. The Body of Christ is none of them.',
